Prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area as referred to in Article 70 letter a shall be implemented through:
a. implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the prevention of VAC involving parties in the Regency Area;
b. provision of education on VAC prevention activities involving parties in the Regency Area;
c. enhancement of the participation of the Community, Business World, media, and Children in the prevention of VAC in the Regency Area; andd. strengthening cooperation to realize CFC, child-friendly sub-districts, and child-friendly Villages/sub-districts.

Article 25

1. The Regency Regional Government provides services to women as referred to in Article 23 paragraph (3) letter b.
2. The provision of services as referred to in paragraph (1), is provided to:a. women victims as a result of Conflict; and b. women victims of Violence.
3. The provision of services to women as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:a. providing Special Protection;
b. providing services to women victims of Violence;
c. providing services for the fulfillment of specific basic needs for women victims as a result of Conflict; andd. improvement of facilities needed by women in Conflict.
4. In the provision of services as referred to in paragraph (1) the Regency Regional Government must provide data on women victims of Conflict in the Region.
5. Special Protection as referred to in paragraph (3) letter a includes efforts to rescue and protect:a. women from experiencing Violence; andb. defenders of women's human rights.
6. The provision of services to women victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (3) letter b includes services for:a. complaints;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. reproductive health;
d. Social Rehabilitation;
e. Social Reintegration; andf. legal assistance and/or accompaniment.
7. Improvement of facilities needed by women in Conflict as referred to in paragraph (3) letter d includes:a. improvement of health service facilities;
b. improvement of reproductive health service facilities;
c. provision …c. provision of shelter and housing that is decent, safe, and Gender Responsive;
d. ease in repairing new housing construction, public facilities and infrastructure; ande. provision of clean water and sanitation for women.

